.TH NCP 1 "October 2026" "ncp 1.0"
.SH NAME
ncp \- network copy: download a URL to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncp
.RB [ \-cq ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.I url
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ncp
downloads
.I url
over HTTP or HTTPS and saves it to a file named after the last part of
the URL path, or
.B index.html
if the path ends in a slash.
Redirects are followed, up to ten.
.PP
HTTPS certificates are verified against
.IR /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt .
If that file does not exist,
.B ncp
prints a warning and does not verify the server.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Continue a partial download, starting from the size of the existing file.
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Save to
.I file
instead of the name taken from the URL.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet: do not show progress. Errors and warnings are still printed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ncp https://www.nano-editor.org/dist/v8/nano-8.6.tar.xz
ncp -c https://example.com/big.iso
ncp -q -o page.html https://example.com/
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cp (1),
.BR wget (1),
.BR curl (1)
